# =====================================================================
# Release V172 -- the data-quality scorecard
# =====================================================================
# Turns the ad-hoc data-quality review into a standing feature: Gold.Aggregate_Data_Quality,
# one row per check per practice, surfaced as a third bookmark view ("Data Quality") on the
# Day Book page beside the existing Diary and Unadopted Patients views.
#
# WHAT IT IS NOT. It does not replace Gold.Dim_Patient_Data_Quality -- that view is the NAMED
# LIST behind "Unadopted Patients" (patients whose assigned clinician has left, or who have no
# dentist at all), and it stays exactly as it is. The scorecard is the layer above: counts,
# severity and what to do about each, across patients, diary, recalls, people and treatments.
# PAT_NO_DENTIST deliberately overlaps that view and its What_To_Do points the reader at it.
#
# ==> PASSING CHECKS MUST STILL PRODUCE A ROW. <== The final SELECT is built catalogue-first --
# tenants CROSS JOIN Config.Data_Quality_Check LEFT JOIN the counts -- so a check with nothing
# to report renders as a visible 0 rather than vanishing. A scorecard that only listed problems
# would be indistinguishable from a scorecard that had failed to run, which is the one way this
# feature could actively mislead a practice.
#
# ==> A CATALOGUE ROW WITH NO COUNTING BRANCH REPORTS 0 FOR EVER. <== Check_Code is the join
# between Config.Data_Quality_Check (wording, severity, guidance) and the UNION ALL of counting
# branches in the load proc. Adding a check means BOTH. A typo in either leaves a row on the
# report permanently reading "clean" -- see the note at the top of both files.
#
# WINDOWS. DIARY_NOT_CLOSED and DIARY_LEFT_OPEN look back 90 days only. Unbounded, the first is
# ~27,000 rows of history on tenant 100 that no practice will ever work through; 90 days is the
# span where setting the real outcome on an appointment is still plausible.
#
# TENANT SPINE comes from Gold.Dim_Patients, so a part-populated test tenant with appointments
# but no patients (tenant 11 on dev) is scored as nothing rather than as a practice failing
# every patient check.
#
# NEW TABLES, so both Table.sql files DEPLOY normally. The usual prohibition on deploying a
# Gold *.Table.sql does not apply here: it exists because DROP TABLE reassigns surrogate keys
# that hash-gated facts still point at, and nothing points at pk_Data_Quality -- the aggregate
# is a full DELETE + INSERT rebuild with no dependants.
#
# AFTER DEPLOYING, IN POWER BI DESKTOP (the model is a .pbix; a new table cannot be added from
# here):
#   1. import PBI.[Aggregate Data Quality]
#   2. add it to the RLS role, filtering [Tenant ID] the same way as every other table --
#      Scripts\Check_RLS_Coverage.ps1 fails the build if this is missed, and a miss is a
#      cross-tenant leak
#   3. save + publish, then open Day Book -- the new "Data Quality" bookmark appears on the
#      navigator by itself
#
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V172__data_quality_scorecard.manifest
# =====================================================================

# The check catalogue: wording, severity and guidance, owner-curated. Deployed before the
# aggregate because the load proc CROSS JOINs it -- an empty catalogue produces an empty
# scorecard with no error.
DEPLOY   Fabric\Config.Data_Quality_Check.Table.sql
DEPLOY   Fabric\Config.Data_Quality_Check.Data.sql

DEPLOY   Fabric\Gold.Aggregate_Data_Quality.Table.sql
DEPLOY   Fabric\Gold.usp_Load_Aggregate_Data_Quality.StoredProcedure.sql

# Registers GOLD_AGG_DATA_QUALITY in the DAG so the nightly build runs it. The dependency file
# is GENERATED -- it was rebuilt by Scripts\Generate_Process_Dependencies.ps1, not hand-edited,
# and it places the new aggregate at level 5, after the six Gold objects it reads.
DEPLOY   Fabric\Audit.Process_Config.Data.sql
DEPLOY   Fabric\Audit.Process_Dependency.Data.sql

EXEC     DECLARE @i BIGINT,@u BIGINT,@d BIGINT; EXEC Gold.usp_Load_Aggregate_Data_Quality @Mode='PROD',@Run_Inserts=@i OUT,@Run_Updates=@u OUT,@Run_Deletes=@d OUT;
EXEC     EXEC Meta.usp_Create_Gold_Views;

TEST
